<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/claim/morphoeval-grieneisen-root-auxin-reflux-fountain> a pk:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "Grieneisen et al. (2007) Nature & Mähönen et al. (2014) Nature reverse-fountain root tip auxin reflux capacitor, Quiescent Center exponential accumulation, and PLETHORA meristem zonality (Arabidopsis thaliana (primary root apex: vascular stele, pericycle/endodermis, cortex, epidermis/lateral root cap, quiescent center, and columella))",
        "Grieneisen et al. (2007) Nature & Mähönen et al. (2014) Nature reverse-fountain root tip auxin reflux capacitor, Quiescent Center exponential accumulation, and PLETHORA meristem zonality faithfully reproduces Arabidopsis thaliana (primary root apex: vascular stele, pericycle/endodermis, cortex, epidermis/lateral root cap, quiescent center, and columella) morphology" ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/grieneisen-root-auxin-reflux-fountain-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/grieneisen-root-auxin-reflux-fountain-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/grieneisen-root-auxin-reflux-fountain-3> ;
    dct:description "The simulation script(s) 2014-grieneisen-root-auxin-reflux-fountain.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Arabidopsis thaliana (primary root apex: vascular stele, pericycle/endodermis, cortex, epidermis/lateral root cap, quiescent center, and columella) specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is the weight of evidence (MorphoEval 0.1.0 overall 93.2/100, audit 2026-10-19-root-auxin-reflux-fountain-audit-v2) and the assessments." ;
    dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/8871db0/2014-grieneisen-root-auxin-reflux-fountain.py> ;
    schema:about "Arabidopsis thaliana (primary root apex: vascular stele, pericycle/endodermis, cortex, epidermis/lateral root cap, quiescent center, and columella)" ;
    schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: Subcellular cell-wall mechanical viscoplasticity or 3D gravitropic root bending curvature",
        "reconstructed_in_script: 2D 5-tissue root tip cellular lattice solver (32 axial rows x 9 radial files: epidermis/LRC, cortex, endodermis/pericycle, stele, and distal columella/QC) verifying counter-current vascular-epidermal flux conservation (error 2e-15 <= 1e-12) and reproducing all 6 experimental regimes: Wild-Type (132.05x QC amplification at z=37.5 um), shoot decapitation J_in=0 autonomy (115.56x, retaining 87.5% of WT peak), pin2/eir1 mutant (54.1x, z_MZ=210 um), lateral-PIN ablation k_lat=0 (10.38x, z_MZ=90 um), NPA blockade (1.31x, z_MZ=0 um), and QC laser ablation regenerating a proximal QC peak at z=97.5 um (+60 um shift)",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Coupled PLETHORA (PLT1/2) reaction-diffusion-dilution solver achieving Pearson r = 0.9929 (p = 7.47e-5) against published Meristematic Zone boundaries across all 6 perturbation regimes and r = 0.9851 along the WT axial profile",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Empirical CV segmentation of the 3-panel Arabidopsis thaliana primary root meristem confocal micrograph (`arabidopsis_root_meristem_specimen.jpg`, CC BY-SA 4.0, 1527x513 px) extracting root meristem area fraction (0.2561), N = 113 DAPI-stained nuclei (intercellular spacing 18.3394 +- 0.5790 px SE), N = 125 Alexa Fluor 488 mitotic phragmoplast/spindle divisions, and apical-to-proximal nuclear density ratio (1.1182)",
        "reported_in_source: Grieneisen, Xu, Marée, Hogeweg & Scheres (2007) Nature 449:1008-1013 2D multi-file root apex reverse-fountain auxin reflux loop (downward PIN1 stele transport +v_s, lateral PIN3/PIN4/PIN7 columella/QC redistribution, upward PIN2 epidermal/LRC transport -v_e, and inward lateral PIN1/PIN2/PIN3 reflux k_lat across cortex/endodermis), generating an exponential Quiescent Center (QC) auxin capacitor (>100-fold peak) that remains self-sustaining after shoot decapitation (J_in = 0) and regenerates a shifted proximal QC peak after distal laser ablation",
        "reported_in_source: Mähönen et al. (2014) Nature 515:125-129 slow auxin-induced PLETHORA (PLT1/PLT2) transcription factor synthesis, cell-to-cell movement, and growth dilution creating a smooth axial PLT dosage gradient that positions Meristematic Zone (P >= Theta_MZ), Elongation Zone (Theta_EZ <= P < Theta_MZ), and Differentiation Zone (P < Theta_EZ) boundaries",
        "transfer_boundary: 2D radial-axial 5-tissue cellular root apex reflux capacitor and PLETHORA dosage thresholds mapped to confocal Arabidopsis root meristem nuclear and mitotic architecture" ;
    pk:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/8871db0/2014-grieneisen-root-auxin-reflux-fountain.py; output: docs/media/root_auxin_reflux_fountain_comparison.png; organism: Arabidopsis thaliana (primary root apex: vascular stele, pericycle/endodermis, cortex, epidermis/lateral root cap, quiescent center, and columella); checkpoint commit: https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/commit/8871db0; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.4.2, scipy 1.17.0, matplotlib 3.10.8, Pillow 12.1.1; spec_fingerprint: 5f9ff984dd3572c3a2bb1124d68b38a94c8ae92664796e5dd367404918a3bd5f; artifact_sha256: 12e908c56deebba7631ec0c11c4291b5a4c995e66a43e76a97072750537346c4; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/root_auxin_reflux_fountain/arabidopsis_root_meristem_specimen.jpg=1b962c21e75c8e72..., datasets/root_auxin_reflux_fountain/paper_citations.bib=069ef06b9ad6bdfb..., datasets/root_auxin_reflux_fountain/root_auxin_reflux_fountain_reference.json=1fc68ce109094fc5..., datasets/root_auxin_reflux_fountain/scout_manifest.json=285fff11a61df708...}; supersedes_audit_id: 2026-10-19-root-auxin-reflux-fountain-audit; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Grieneisen, Xu, Marée, Hogeweg & Scheres (2007) Nature 449:1008-1013 2D multi-file root apex reverse-fountain auxin reflux loop (downward PIN1 stele transport +v_s, lateral PIN3/PIN4/PIN7 columella/QC redistribution, upward PIN2 epidermal/LRC transport -v_e, and inward lateral PIN1/PIN2/PIN3 reflux k_lat across cortex/endodermis), generating an exponential Quiescent Center (QC) auxin capacitor (>100-fold peak) that remains self-sustaining after shoot decapitation (J_in = 0) and regenerates a shifted proximal QC peak after distal laser ablation | Mähönen et al. (2014) Nature 515:125-129 slow auxin-induced PLETHORA (PLT1/PLT2) transcription factor synthesis, cell-to-cell movement, and growth dilution creating a smooth axial PLT dosage gradient that positions Meristematic Zone (P >= Theta_MZ), Elongation Zone (Theta_EZ <= P < Theta_MZ), and Differentiation Zone (P < Theta_EZ) boundaries; reconstructed_in_script: 2D 5-tissue root tip cellular lattice solver (32 axial rows x 9 radial files: epidermis/LRC, cortex, endodermis/pericycle, stele, and distal columella/QC) verifying counter-current vascular-epidermal flux conservation (error 2e-15 <= 1e-12) and reproducing all 6 experimental regimes: Wild-Type (132.05x QC amplification at z=37.5 um), shoot decapitation J_in=0 autonomy (115.56x, retaining 87.5% of WT peak), pin2/eir1 mutant (54.1x, z_MZ=210 um), lateral-PIN ablation k_lat=0 (10.38x, z_MZ=90 um), NPA blockade (1.31x, z_MZ=0 um), and QC laser ablation regenerating a proximal QC peak at z=97.5 um (+60 um shift) | Coupled PLETHORA (PLT1/2) reaction-diffusion-dilution solver achieving Pearson r = 0.9929 (p = 7.47e-5) against published Meristematic Zone boundaries across all 6 perturbation regimes and r = 0.9851 along the WT axial profile | Empirical CV segmentation of the 3-panel Arabidopsis thaliana primary root meristem confocal micrograph (`arabidopsis_root_meristem_specimen.jpg`, CC BY-SA 4.0, 1527x513 px) extracting root meristem area fraction (0.2561), N = 113 DAPI-stained nuclei (intercellular spacing 18.3394 +- 0.5790 px SE), N = 125 Alexa Fluor 488 mitotic phragmoplast/spindle divisions, and apical-to-proximal nuclear density ratio (1.1182); transfer_boundary: 2D radial-axial 5-tissue cellular root apex reflux capacitor and PLETHORA dosage thresholds mapped to confocal Arabidopsis root meristem nuclear and mitotic architecture; does_not_claim: Subcellular cell-wall mechanical viscoplasticity or 3D gravitropic root bending curvature]" ;
    pk:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1016/S0092-8674(00)81535-4>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/nature03184>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/nature06215>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/nature13663> ;
    pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-grieneisen-root-auxin-reflux-fountain-code-traceability>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-grieneisen-root-auxin-reflux-fountain-model-fidelity>,
